{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3903","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3903","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3903\",\"parent_revision\":\"04fa90060b86e3fcb9dfa8c9190e25f20ff93b8b9555f15ed7fde2031b188cd1\",\"root_revision\":\"04fa90060b86e3fcb9dfa8c9190e25f20ff93b8b9555f15ed7fde2031b188cd1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Requested Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nProvide Development Harness guidance for planning meaningful software tests before writing them (including each TDD increment), and for reviewing existing tests against the product behavior they actually exercise. Determine whether a test protects a justified, important claim rather than treating execution, coverage, test counts, or a green suite as proof of value.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope And Integration\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBuild on PR #3900's contract-driven review/investigation work, without changing its causal-tracing or Python implementation guidance. Add language-independent `test-designer` and `test-reviewer` skills; preserve `comprehensive-test-review` as an existing entry point to the shared review process. Language plugins continue to own implementation specialists and framework-specific testing details.\\n\\nStore the shared testing principles once inside the DH plugin. Cover stable behavioral contracts, discriminating faults, independent oracles, refactor tolerance, faithful boundaries/test doubles, consequence-based rigor, transitions/forbidden effects, controlled experiments, diagnostics, and suite maintenance. Respect existing project gates without inventing universal coverage percentages or one-test-per-symbol rules.\\n\\nThe reviewer must trace assertions to product behavior and report justified keep/strengthen/replace/consolidate/removal-candidate or unresolved dispositions. It must not delete tests merely because a requirement is hard to find or another test has a similar name. Characterization, freshness, integration, and behavioral guarantees require distinct evidence.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Plan And Acceptance\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Add shared source-backed principles and a compact test-design/review contract.\\n- [ ] Add portable planning and read-only review skills with short, stable capability goals.\\n- [ ] Connect planning/task handoffs and existing review entry points without changing SAM schemas or specialist resolution.\\n- [ ] Preserve PR #3900's guarantees, including safe negative controls, skips/xfails/selection reporting, generated-artifact distinctions, and explicit unvalidated outcomes.\\n- [ ] Add discriminating evaluation scenarios, including meaningful TDD red, vacuous tests, legitimate interaction assertions, overlap at different boundaries, and unsafe/missing evidence.\\n- [ ] Validate available artifact properties and published content; distinguish static checks, remote CI, and unexecuted agent evaluations.\\n- [ ] Open a focused PR and record its dependency on #3900.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence Boundaries\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nLocal cloning failed with `Could not resolve host: github.com`; the GitHub connector works. This environment has no discovered Claude/Codex executable for fresh-agent evaluation. Do not represent authored scenarios or static source checks as successful agent execution. Workflow graph refresh has a documented retired extractor/pending redesign; record affected graph coverage instead of hand-editing generated layer/graph data.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5d691ccb6379c2d8e635f5029b42bd844bf2ab184a9d8acae8d9dbc3c42e1e5b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCLP4g\"}"}